text:
@matkarsachinguys he is not talking to just use the interest, also consumer the 50% capital invested in FD. He divided the 3cr in two parts, part 1 is consumed in 20 years with whatever interest it earns on reducing balance. The interest income keeps reducing and capital consumption continues to increase as you go further in time. 

The part 2 is invested in market. Assuming that the market performs as he expects.. it’s also possible that the market looses value or remains stagnant

My issue is that he has not taken inflation into account. 1.5 cr today is worth significantly less 10 years from now
